-- title:
--   Evaluated Slice Phase Two Question Defect Append Eq Sum Poly
-- statement:
--   **Polynomial-outcome expansion of the phase-two question defect.**
--
--   Let `params` be the test parameters, `strategy` a symmetric projective strategy, `family` an indexed polynomial submeasurement, and `G` the slice polynomial family. For $q_1\in\mathbb{F}_q^{m+1}$, $v\in\mathbb{F}_q^m$, and $y\in\mathbb{F}_q$, evaluating the phase-two defect at the appended point and expanding the outcome fibers gives
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{phaseTwoQuestionDefect}\left(q_1,\operatorname{appendPoint}(v,y)\right)=\sum_g\sum_a\operatorname{ev}_\psi\left(\left(G^{q_1}_aG^y_gG^{q_1}_a\left(I-G^y_{\mathrm{total}}\right)\right)\otimes P^{\operatorname{appendPoint}(v,y)}_{g(v)}\right).
--   $$
--
--   The symbols $G^{q_1}_a$, $G^y_g$, and $P^{\operatorname{appendPoint}(v,y)}_{g(v)}$ denote the evaluated family and strategy effects. This reindexing makes the polynomial outcome explicit for the phase-two reduction.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.evaluatedSlicePhaseTwoQuestionDefect_append_eq_sum_poly`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
